IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-employee`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1958 (WA), ss 4A, 5, 6, 6A, 7-7C, 7E-7H, 8, 9, 10, 26A, 27 -- worked cases from the seat of the
-- employee.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case, an industrial magistrate's decision or Wageline guidance (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_wa_long-service-leave-act-1958_baseline.py). Expected results
-- were written by hand from the text. 8 2/3 weeks is written 26/3; 4 1/3 weeks is 13/3.
--
-- THE LIVES. c056 (2029-09-02): Liam Nguyen, electrician (apprenticeship 2017-2021), leaves his employer for another.
-- c072 (2034-02-01): Chloe Harding leaves Ironbark Logistics (employed 5 February 2024 to 31 January 2034) for Jarrah
-- Legal Technologies. Where the facts do not settle a figure (Liam's years with his old employer; Chloe's unpaid
-- parental leave; their weekly pay), the case says which figure it assumes.

§ `s 4A -- does the Act apply to me`

#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 6, 6A -- continuous employment`

`paid annual leave` MEANS AbsenceFacts WITH
    `the absence` IS `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)`
    `it was paid` IS TRUE
    `I am a casual or seasonal employee` IS FALSE
    `I came back as soon as practicable` IS FALSE
    `I returned on the terms that settled the dispute` IS FALSE
    `my employer gave written notice within 14 days that continuity was broken` IS FALSE
    `months until my employer re-employed me` IS 0
    `the dismissal was for slackness of trade` IS FALSE
    `if the dismissal was made to avoid long service leave or annual leave` IS FALSE

`unpaid parental leave` MEANS AbsenceFacts WITH
    `the absence` IS `leave of a kind listed in s 6(1)`
    `it was paid` IS FALSE
    `I am a casual or seasonal employee` IS FALSE
